	doi = {10.4324/9780203998045},
	abstract = {In this chapter we review recent progress in developing computational (connectionist) models of numerical cognition. We focus on three main issues: (a) number representations, (b) basic numerical skills (number comparison, subitizing, counting), and (c) simple mental arithmetic. We first review the previous attempts to model human numerical skills. We then present our comprehensive theoretical proposal, which revolves around the notion of numerosity representations. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)},
